 ## Background
-This method originates from the need for efficient and robust pose estimation in neural implicit representations. It builds on the principles of Lie group optimization, where updates are performed in the tangent space to maintain the manifold structure [S1, S2]. The specific formulation using the tangent plane for $SE(3)$ optimization was highlighted in [S2] as superior to direct manifold optimization for avoiding noisy photometric loss landscapes. The approach is used in systems like Vox-Fusion for dense tracking and mapping [S1] and LATITUDE for robotic global localization [S2].
